# structgen arguments for sdk/ts/gen/oracle_layout.oracle_mt.ts: the Infinite
# Oracle's Mode B reader of the candidate table oracle-mt.wasm publishes
# (c/src/oracle_mt.h OgMtCandidates). A snapshot reader only, like the client's
# view readers. Read by tools/structgen/gen.sh with --cwd c/ and the oracle-mt
# build's own flags (the header is compiled only under FOOLISH_ORACLE_MT).
# Lines starting with # are dropped; everything else is split on whitespace.
--header oracle_mt.h --root OgMtCandidates
--snapshot OgMtCandidates --snapshot-only
--count OgMtCandidates.cand=n --count OgMtCand.cards=n_cards --count OgMtCand.targets=n_targets
# And the knobs the Oracle sets before a job (c/src/oracle_answer.h OgKnobs),
# which go in through their writer in both oracle modules: Mode A's is in
# specs/oracle_answer.args.
--header oracle_answer.h --root OgKnobs --snapshot OgKnobs --writer OgKnobs
